  "generated_text": "To determine the least possible number of students who have both brown eyes and a lunch box, we need to consider the principle of inclusion studentsclusion. the..\n\n1. Let \\( B \\) be the set of students with brown eyes.\n2. Let \\( L \\) be the set of students with a lunch box.\n3. We know \\( |B| = 12 \\) and \\( |L| = 20 \\).\n4. The total number of students in the class is 30.\n\nUsing the principle of inclusion-exclusion, we have:\n\\[ |BB \\ L L| = |B + + |L - - |B \\cap L| \\]\n\nSubstituting the known values:\n\\[ 30 = 12 + 20 - |B \\cap L| \\]\n\nSolving for \\( |B \\cap L| \\):\n\\[ 30 = 32 - |B \\cap L| \\]\n\\[ |B \\cap L| = 32 - 30 = 2 \\]\n\nTherefore, the least possible number of students who have both brown eyes and a lunch box is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
  "grade": {
